task: async-direct-loop (Drive.apply as a direct loop over Free, Run/Await inlined; measured before/after)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/async-direct-loop

why: free-bind-node-count (§18b) measured runAsync's round-trip at
  12.6 us of bind_runAsync's 40.2 on the JVM (bind_runWith, already a
  direct loop via runFree, reads 27.6), and an unknown share of the
  300 us of injection on Native, where BenchCross runs runAsync. The
  precedent is in-tree: runFree (Effects.scala) and Stm's runner match
  Free's cases directly with the effect's operations inlined, no
  polymorphic handler value, no closure per step. Drive.apply gets the
  same shape; the Await exchange cell and cancellation-at-next-
  operation stay exactly as they are. Measured on bind_runAsync (JMH,
  -prof gc) and bindChain on Native and JS before/after. Not a change
  to Free, fold, runFree, or any other handler.
